Save this as .mcp.json in a folder of its own that you use only for calendar work. Claude Code asks once before it uses a server from .mcp.json. Do not add the entry for the user (--scope user), and do not put it into the Fabric repository or a folder above it.

{
  "mcpServers": {
    "fabric-calendar": {
      "command": "/Applications/Fabric Calendar.app/Contents/MacOS/fabric-mcp-bridge",
      "args": ["--enrollment", "agent-0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef"]
    }
  }
}

The same entry can be added from that folder with:
claude mcp add --scope project fabric-calendar -- '/Applications/Fabric Calendar.app/Contents/MacOS/fabric-mcp-bridge' --enrollment agent-0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef

